      "kind": "image_ocr",
      "text": "01\nLight is\nimportant\nfor sleep\nNewborn sleep is naturally\nfragmented because the\nday-night rhythm is still\ndeveloping.\nAround 6-12 weeks, babies\nbegin to tell day from night.\nLight is an important\ntime cue to develop the\nday-night rhythm.\nDuring the day\nLight signals the brain to suppress melatonin,\nhelping us stay alert.\nlight\nEyes\nRetina\nRHT\nRetino-hypothalamic\ntract\nSCN\nSuprachiasmatic\nnucleus\nExcited\nMelatonin\nPineal body\nAt night\nMelatonin production rises,\nhelping us feel sleepy.",
